  "worked_solution": "We have $\\frac{4}{7}$ on the left and $\\frac{4}{14}$ on the right.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133144/assets/9a2f2136b843a54c3038b2905570d1932b2547279953093f3b6c89fc65d4b11b.png)\n\nThe division operation splits each vertical line into $2$ equal parts. So the shaded parts on the left are $2$ times larger than the shaded parts on the right.  \n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{7}÷2=\\frac{4}{14}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $2.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
